.TH "HTMLTABLEELEMENT.INSERTROW" "3JS" "August 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLTableElement.insertRow \- HTMLTableElement: insertRow() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]insertRow()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]HTMLTableElement\f[R] interface creates a \f[CR]<tr>\f[R] element,
inserts it at the specified position in the \f[CR]rows\f[R] collection,
and returns it.
If the \f[CR]rows\f[R] collection is empty and the table also has no
\f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] elements, a \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] element is first
created and inserted.
.PP
This method creates and inserts the element directly, without requiring
separate calls to methods such as \f[CR]Document.createElement()\f[R],
\f[CR]Node.insertBefore()\f[R], and \f[CR]Node.appendChild()\f[R].
.PP
To explicitly insert a row into a specific section, use
\f[CR]HTMLTableSectionElement.insertRow()\f[R].
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
insertRow()
insertRow(index)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]index\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
The index of the new row in the \f[CR]rows\f[R] collection.
If \f[CR]index\f[R] is \f[CR]\-1\f[R] or equal to the number of rows,
the row is appended as the last row.
If \f[CR]index\f[R] is omitted, it defaults to \f[CR]\-1\f[R].
.RS
.PP
If \f[CR]rows\f[R] is empty, the new row is appended to the last
\f[CR]<tbody>\f[R] element (one is created if there\(cqs none).
Otherwise, the new row is inserted immediately before the row at
\f[CR]index\f[R], or appended to the parent of the last row if the new
row is to become the last row.
The new row is inserted into the same parent as the reference row, so it
can be inserted directly into the \f[CR]<table>\f[R] or into any table
sectioning element (\f[CR]<thead>\f[R], \f[CR]<tbody>\f[R], or
\f[CR]<tfoot>\f[R]).
.RE
.SS Return value
An \f[CR]HTMLTableRowElement\f[R] that references the new row.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]IndexSizeError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if \f[CR]index\f[R] is greater than the number of rows or smaller
than \f[CR]\-1\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
This example uses \f[CR]insertRow(\-1)\f[R] to append a new row to a
table.
.PP
We then use \f[CR]HTMLTableRowElement.insertCell()\f[R] to insert a new
cell in the new row.
Finally, we add some text to the cell using
\f[CR]Document.createTextNode()\f[R] and \f[CR]Node.appendChild()\f[R].
.SS HTML
.IP
.EX
<\f[B]table\f[R] id=\(dqmy\-table\(dq>
  <\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Row 1</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Row 2</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
    <\f[B]tr\f[R]>
      <\f[B]td\f[R]>Row 3</\f[B]td\f[R]>
    </\f[B]tr\f[R]>
  </\f[B]tbody\f[R]>
</\f[B]table\f[R]>
.EE
.SS JavaScript
.IP
.EX
\f[B]function\f[R] addRow(tableID) {
  \f[I]// Get a reference to the table\f[R]
  \f[B]const\f[R] tableRef = document.getElementById(tableID);

  \f[I]// Insert a row at the end of the table\f[R]
  \f[B]const\f[R] newRow = tableRef.insertRow(\-1);

  \f[I]// Insert a cell in the row at index 0\f[R]
  \f[B]const\f[R] newCell = newRow.insertCell(0);

  \f[I]// Append a text node to the cell\f[R]
  \f[B]const\f[R] newText = document.createTextNode(\(dqNew bottom row\(dq);
  newCell.appendChild(newText);
}

\f[I]// Call addRow() with the table\(aqs ID\f[R]
addRow(\(dqmy\-table\(dq);
.EE
.SS Result
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]HTMLTableRowElement.insertCell()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]HTMLTableSectionElement.insertRow()\f[R]
